        "id": 19646,
        "name": "Armisael",
        "username": "Armisael",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/a/5fc32e/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2019-12-26T20:58:40.000Z",
        "cooked": "<ol>\n\t<li>I'm playing as Serpent and I play <a href=\"https://sick.oberien.de/imgs/powers/unrelenting_growth.webp\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">Unrelenting Growth</a> on myself. One of the presence I lay uncovers an any on my track. Can I use that any to meet the elemental threshold for Unrelenting Growth?</li>\n\t<li>My event card for the turn includes Stricken (Invaders do not ravage in lands with disease/strife). The fear cards instructs me to add a strife to a land, and I add one to a land that would be ravaging (ie, the right land type and did not already have strife or disease). Does it ravage (because it didn't have a strife when the event card activated) or does it not ravage (because it has a strife when the Ravage comes around)?</li>\n</ol>\n<p>Thanks!&nbsp;</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:53:24.488Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
        "quote_count": 0,
